## Timeline logic
- AWS DPA text born 2026-06-04; merge 2026-06-09; activation not yet.
- "Implementation" for DPA purposes = customer data flowing = flag enablement, which hasn't happened. So the §8.1 14-day window can still be satisfied: confirm/send notice → enable flag ≥14 days later.
- DC 9's "deferred more than 30 days after notice" is stronger than the DPA requires (14) and currently unevidenced — soften to "in accordance with the DPA's 14-day subprocessor-change notice" unless 30 days is genuinely observed.

